All &nbsp;Further to Anna’s email please see attached the sealed order, and the letter on ATE / Funding as sent to the Defendants yesterday. &nbsp;Kind regardsJess &nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 24 October 2025 10:56To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.comCc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;Sorry for slow reply and thanks for your comments, which we implemented. The letter was sent yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please note that the deadline for Ds to renew applications and/or make new ones is today and we can safely assume there will be bit of a deluge on that front.&nbsp;&nbsp;@Jessica Fechner&nbsp;please could you share the now sealed order and the letter as sent.&nbsp;&nbsp;We will also update about ATE top-up, timings etc.&nbsp;ThanksAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: Thursday, October 23, 2025 12:43 PMTo: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi all,&nbsp;Sorry I am in court today so timings are tricky.&nbsp;Having considered overnight In my view it would be better (as you have also concluded) not to say anything yet about additional ATE until you’ve got it sorted.&nbsp;I wouldn’t use the phrase “would be meritless and designed to distract from the substantive proceedings” in para 3. That is putting it too high. The Ds expectation of security is legitimate. Our point is they are sufficiently secured. To say the proposed application is ‘meritless’ is not a great idea when we know we are about to get additional ATE. I think you should say “would fail” instead.&nbsp;I cannot work out what the reference to Willers v Joyce was supposed to be to. I agree the now-referenced case doesn’t look on point either. I suggest leaving out this paragraph and asking whoever drafted the original letter whether they meant a different case.&nbsp;I would delete para 8 because we know that this isn’t going to bring matters to a close!&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our&nbsp;Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Thursday, 23 October 2025 at 12:09To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;, Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;, Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2EXTERNAL EMAILDear Theo &nbsp;Recognising that we have asked for a quick turnaround on this one, please could I check when you think you might be able to provide your views on the draft letter (re-attached)? &nbsp;We confirm we are still keen to send this today. &nbsp;Many thanks in advance for your input. &nbsp;Kind RegardsJess&nbsp;Jessica Fechner (she/her)Associate (England &amp; Wales qualified) Amsterdam &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Please note that our general terms and conditions apply to all our services. These general terms and conditions include a clause stipulating that our liability is excluded for damage caused by an event not covered by any insurance. The full general terms and conditions can be accessed via this link.​​Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of PGMBM Nederland B.V., a limited liability company registered at Chamber of Commerce (no. 83137718) with its registered office at Herengracht 433, 1017 BR Amsterdam. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.​​Deze e-mail en eventuele bijlagen zijn vertrouwelijk. Als u dit bericht ten onrechte ontvangt, neem dan onmiddellijk contact op met de afzender, vernietig de e-mail en eventuele bijlagen en gebruik, kopieer, bewaar of deel deze e-mail en eventuele bijlagen op geen enkele wijze. Pogust Goodhead aanvaardt geen betekening of kennisgeving van documenten langs elektronische weg zonder uitdrukkelijke voorafgaande toestemming.&nbsp;Op alle door Pogust Goodhead aanvaarde opdrachten zijn onze algemene voorwaarden van toepassing. De algemene voorwaarden bevatten onder meer een clausule waarin staat dat onze aansprakelijkheid is uitgesloten voor schade die niet door een verzekering wordt gedekt. De volledige tekst van onze algemene voorwaarden zijn toegankelijk via deze link.​Pogust Goodhead is de handelsnaam van PGMBM Nederland B.V., een naamloze vennootschap ingeschreven bij de Kamer van Koophandel (nr. 83137718), statutair gevestigd aan de Herengracht 433, 1017 BR Amsterdam. Voor meer informatie over welke persoonsgegeven wij verzamelen en waarom, zie onze Privacy Policy.From: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 22 October 2025 21:13To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.comCc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Both &nbsp;See below analysis of the topup in adverse costs cover that we have asked our brokers to arrange:&nbsp;LOI topup analysis&nbsp;DefendantAdverse Costs Exposure (to Jul 26)LOI in placeSurplus / (Shortfall)Topup requiredAs % LOIMercedes11,057,0848,454,172-2,602,9112,602,91131%Ford14,810,00911,105,133-3,704,8763,704,87633%RN24,897,73018,550,234-6,347,4966,347,49634%Citroen-Peugeot9,630,5678,115,744-1,514,8231,514,82319%BMW3,933,7055,000,0001,066,29500%FCA8,785,7158,205,964-579,751579,7517%JLR2,809,8372,821,40811,57100%Hyundai-Kia1,854,8171,677,429-177,389177,38911%VW2 Porsche6,959,6757,141,252181,57700%Vauxhall1,909,2492,000,00090,75100%Volvo1,674,5055,000,0003,325,49500%Mazda2,688,2812,685,173-3,1083,1080%Toyota3,422,3242,951,874-470,450470,45016%Total94,433,49883,708,383-10,725,11515,400,80318%&nbsp;This would provide sufficient indemnity to cover the claimant’s cost exposure to 31 July 2026, as per the assumptions outlined in Anna’s email (Increasing the T3 trial prep assumption to 50% would add £1.4m total LOI to the above).&nbsp;The brokers have indicated that they are able to provide a quote for some of the required topup by the end of the week, exact amounts per manufacturer will be provided tomorrow. &nbsp;It is not clear on the timing or certainty of availability of the remainder of the topup as the brokers have to approach the open market. I expect to have an update on this position tomorrow also. &nbsp;Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 22 October 2025 20:31To: T.Barclay@4newsquare.com; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.comCc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Theo&nbsp;See below a break down of the additional cover that is being sought - this aligns with the approach Leigh Day is taking. I don't yet have pro rated cover per defendant: @Tom Crow&nbsp;is that something you could assist with please?&nbsp;60% of the Defendants incurred costs (including those from CMH1 and CMH2, the costs of cost budgeting from both CMH1 and CMH2, and the Non-Tranche 3 Quantum costs).100% of the Defendants Tranche 2 (£90.5 million) and First General approved future costs (£19.25 million)Defendants Tranche 3 approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:100% of CMC, Selection of Sample Claimants, Individual Statements of Case, Disclosure, Witness Statements, and PTR71% of the Tranche 3 Co-Ordination Costs (12.5 out of 17.5 months)Trial Preparation: We had been considering seeking between 33% and 50%. However, Leigh Day is seeking 50%, and we consider a more conservative approach is appropriate in light of the scrutiny. If we go with 50% this would add c. £1.5 million LOI which we can accommodate in the budget. &nbsp;Defendants Second General approved future costs up to 31 July 2026, broken down as follows:44% of GLO Management CostsFortnightly Meetings to September 2026 at 67%T3 Expert Reports/2G ADR: Figures based on Claimant offers. 100% of £10.2m for expert reports, and 44% of £1.8m for ADR. Leigh Day have based their approach on agreed figures, with the following exceptions: &nbsp;where not agreed, Defendants counteroffer, and where no counteroffer, Claimants offer).&nbsp;BestAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:08 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: B.Williams@4newsquare.com &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you let me know how much further ate cover you are planning to get and what the total pro rated cover per defendant solicitors firm is anticipated to be? That makes &nbsp;a&nbsp;difference, I think, to whether we should say more. If we anticipate getting very close to eliminating the shortfalls, then I would be more in favour of saying so. If we are still going to be way off, it’s probably less good an idea.&nbsp;Thanks&nbsp;Theo &nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOSTheo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our&nbsp;Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 22, 2025 8:02:14 PMTo: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2 &nbsp;EXTERNAL EMAILTheo&nbsp;Please find attached draft response - grateful if you could consider and comment.&nbsp;&nbsp;Note 2 specific queries:&nbsp;1. Re confirming we are seeking additional cover. This is in hand but we don't yet have timings etc. See my comment 