re is a strong case for downgrading the % of incurred costs by 10%. Again, if this is to go into the letter we ought to treat it internally as a holding position while you look to increase cover.&nbsp;We agree that it is not sensible to disclose in the letter that you are looking to increase cover. Most importantly, that essentially amounts to a concession that what you have is insufficient - and additionally, as you point out, you may not be able to secure further cover and we don’t want to box ourselves in.&nbsp;I hope that helps. I am around tomorrow morning if needed until around 1pm.&nbsp;Many thanks,&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Theo&nbsp;Barclay​​​​BarristerDirect&nbsp;+442078222100&nbsp;Mobile&nbsp;+447411&nbsp;731074&nbsp;Chambers&nbsp;+442078222000&nbsp;4&nbsp;New&nbsp;Square&nbsp;Chambers​Lincoln's&nbsp;Inn,&nbsp;London&nbsp;WC2A&nbsp;3RJFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;YouTube | LinkedIn​Discover&nbsp;our Events&nbsp;Privilege and Confidentiality Notice:This email is private as between the sender and the intended recipient. The information contained in this message and any file that may be attached to it are confidential between those parties and may be privileged. Any other party who receives it in error is not permitted to read, use, copy, discuss or pass on the information contained in either the message or its attachments, nor are they entitled to take any action in reliance on the contents. Therefore, if you are not the intended recipient you are kindly requested to contact me immediately by telephone on the numbers given above.Members of 4 New Square Chambers are regulated by the Bar Standards Board.NOTE TO SOLICITORS: ALL PAPERS RECEIVED FOR MEMBERS OF CHAMBERS WILL BE SENT FOR SECURE SHREDDING&nbsp;UPON COMPLETION OF WORK&nbsp;UNLESS YOU SPECIFICALLY REQUEST THEIR RETURN.From: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Thursday, 9 October 2025 at 19:39To: Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;, Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Cc: Benjamin