 subject to PG’s supervision at all times regarding any work you do (delegated Common Work or otherwise); and (b) PG authorises you to do Common Work under the direction of and reporting to LD as LS.&nbsp; We have removed the word “solely” in both cases,
 to make clear that PG continues to supervise and be responsible for you.
&nbsp;
PG have taken specialist employment law advice. The agreement, and what you are being asked to do, is consistent with your employment agreements
 and your rights as employees.
&nbsp;
We have not accepted your proposal that PG personnel can also take direction from a third party authorised by LD. We can discuss this further,
 but PG needs to maintain knowledge and meaningful involvement/control over who can give directions to its personnel – and this is right now limited to LD in its capacity as Lead Solicitor, and a firm with which we have worked significantly on this matter.
 LD is content with this, and it should not raise any concerns regarding your workstreams. &nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As concerns asking junior members of staff to send out correspondence, there is nothing inappropriate about this - and while ideally correspondence
 would be sent out during business hours, that is not out of the ordinary on NOX.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
As already noted, I will share the final version. I hope you are clear and satisfied that we have taken all your comments into account as appropriate
 in order to reach a viable framework for PG’s ongoing role. Agreeing the Agency Agreement is clearly now a priority in order to ensure clarity on next steps for the PDD trial and the proper framework in the best interests of our clients. To be clear, while
 we welcome and value your input, we do not consider that we need your consent to enter into the agreement with Leigh Day.
&nbsp;
We have all discussed this a good deal in writing. I suggest we have a call about this tomorrow and before speaking with Leigh Day. Could you
 let me know when might work?&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
It remains for me to thank you again for all your enormous efforts to get this case to where it is today. We look forward to continuing to work
 together under this framework for the duration of the PDD trial.
