 originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Might lead to requests for the operating budget – and we’d have to give it by virtue of CPR 31.14(1)(b).&nbsp;How about: 37.1: The funds held are made available by Gramercy for PG to draw down in line with its cash needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;Matthew&nbsp;Getz​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1006|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;79&nbsp;8538&nbsp;1095E:&nbsp;&nbsp;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 30 September 2025 15:46To: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Pan-NOx Emissions Group Litigation&nbsp;37.1: The funds are held made available by Gramercy for PG to draw down in line with an operating budget which sets out how the funds can be utilised. &nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Tom&nbsp;CrowGroup&nbsp;Financial&nbsp;Controller+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;708This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-