It’s disappointing to note that you have chosen to resign, given that the Board have listened to concerns which have been raised and has engaged in a process to allay them.&nbsp; We also note the concerns you raise related to the previous leadership
 of the firm. The new Board is determined to bring the highest standards of propriety and integrity to the organisation and is confident that the process being undertaken will arrive at a place that will be in the best interests of the Firm, its employees and,
 most importantly, its clients. Given the above process, your resignation seems premature. As a result, it is with regret, we accept it.
&nbsp;
The Firm notes your request for an early release and your acceptance of your obligations at clause 16 of your resignation letter. Given the deadlines involved in the case you referred to, at this stage, the Firm would like you to continue
